 SDXL and SD1.5 img2img, inpaint and hires fix as Forge runs them
 (modules/processing.py, sd_samplers_kdiffusion.py, sd_samplers_cfg_denoiser.py).

 Resize mode 3 (latent upscale) encodes the picture at its own size and
 resizes the init latent to the request's by torch's bilinear interpolation
 (processing.py:1764, 1818).

 img2img: setup_img2img_steps (sd_samplers_common.py) gives steps and t_enc,
 by default steps and int (min (denoise, 0.999) steps), and for the hires
 pass, which passes its steps, int (steps / min (denoise, 0.999)) and steps
 - 1; the sampler runs the Karras schedule of that many steps from index
 steps - t_enc - 1. The start is the init latent plus noise times the first
 sigma (the eps predictor's noise_scaling). The init latent is the VAE
 posterior's sample, mean + exp (clamp (logvar, -30, 20) / 2) eps, times
 the VAE's scaling factor (vae.py:16-33, process_in). eps is torch.randn on
 the CPU from the global generator (vae.py:27-29), which nothing seeds
 before the encode: its seed is the last rng.randn gave torch.manual_seed,
 (seed + 100000) % 65536 (rng.py:21-23), so a request's own seed from its
 second run on. Under a mask every model call first draws
 torch.randn_like of the init latent from the global CUDA generator, the
 same seed, one draw a call (sd_samplers_cfg_denoiser.py:178-181).

 inpaint: the mask is the picture's alpha thresholded at 128 when it is not
 opaque, else its luma (create_binary_mask; PIL's L is (19595 R + 38470 G +
 7471 B + 32768) >> 16); blurred by cv2.GaussianBlur, kernel 2 int (2.5 blur
 + 0.5) + 1 wide at sigma blur, across then down, reflect-101 borders, at
 the picture's own size; then resized to the request by resize_image with the
 request's mode (processing.py:1739); the overlay mask is twice that, clipped. The latent mask is the blurred mask
 reduced to latent size by PIL's bicubic resize (Resample.c: a = -0.5,
 support 2 times the scale, 22-bit fixed-point coefficients, the horizontal
 pass first, each pass rounded to 8 bits), then rounded: 1 where it is at
 least 128. At every model call the kept region of x is the init latent
 plus fresh noise times sigma, and the kept region of the denoised latent is
 the init latent; the samples are blended the same way at the end. The
 picture pasted back is Pillow's: the original premultiplied by 255 minus
 the overlay mask, unpremultiplied, then alpha-composited over the result.

 hires fix: txt2img at the base size, the latent resized to int (size
 scale) / 8 by torch's bilinear interpolation (align_corners False, no
 antialias; the default "Latent" upscaler), then img2img at the new size
 with its own noise, steps, denoise and CFG; at CFG 1 Forge drops the
 negative prompt and runs the positive alone.

 We say:

Section: Request

  I2i = record {
    i2-base : Txt2Img,
    i2-image : Text,
    i2-mask : Text,
    i2-denoise : Real,
    i2-blur : Integer,
    i2-hr-scale : Real,
    i2-hr-denoise : Real,
    i2-hr-steps : Integer,
    i2-hr-cfg : Real,
    i2-hr-upscaler : Text,
    i2-var : Variation,
    i2-src-w : Integer,
    i2-src-h : Integer,
    i2-resize : Integer,
    i2-fill : Integer,
    i2-area : Integer,
    i2-padding : Integer,
    i2-refiner : Text,
    i2-switch : Real,
    i2-hr-sampler : Integer,
    i2-hr-scheduler : Integer,
    i2-hr-prompt : Text,
    i2-hr-negative : Text,
    i2-hr-ckpt : Text,
    i2-hr-vae : Text,
    i2-soft : Integer,
    i2-sc : SoftCfg,
    i2-out-px : Integer,
    i2-out-blur : Integer,
    i2-out-dirs : Integer,
    i2-post : Integer,
    i2-out-mk2 : Integer,
    i2-out-q : Real,
    i2-out-cv : Real
  }

Section: Floats

  i2-get : Integer, Integer -> Real
  i2-get (a) (i) = un-f32-real (bit-and (peek-32 a (i * 4)) #FFFFFFFF)

  i2-set : Integer, Integer, Real -> Integer
  i2-set (a) (i) (v) = poke-32 a (i * 4) (nz-f32-bits v)

  i2-abs : Real -> Real
  i2-abs (x) = if x < 0.0 then 0.0 - x else x

  i2-floor : Real -> Integer
  i2-floor (x) = let t = real-to-int x in if real-from-int t > x then t - 1 else t

Section: Schedule

  img2img-plan : Integer, Real, Boolean -> List Integer
  img2img-plan (steps) (d) (fixed) =
    let dd = if d < 0.999 then d else 0.999
    in if fixed then [(if d > 0.0 then real-to-int (real-from-int steps / dd) else 0), steps - 1]
    else [steps, real-to-int (dd * real-from-int steps)]

  i2-from : List Real, Integer, List Real -> List Real
  i2-from (xs) (i) (acc) = if i >= list-length xs then acc else i2-from xs (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at xs i))

  i2-karras : Integer -> List Real
  i2-karras (n) =
    if n == 1 then [sm-pow (sm-pow (sm-discrete-sigma 999) (1.0 / 7.0)) 7.0, 0.0]
    else sdxl-karras-sigmas n

  img2img-sigmas : Integer, Real, Boolean -> List Real
  img2img-sigmas (steps) (d) (fixed) =
    let p = img2img-plan steps d fixed
    in let s = list-at p 0
    in i2-from (i2-karras s) (s - list-at p 1 - 1) []

 The same tail of the request's sampler's sigmas under its schedule.

  img2img-sigmas-for : Txt2Img, Boolean, Integer, Real, Boolean -> List Real
  img2img-sigmas-for (r) (sd15) (steps) (d) (fixed) =
    let p = img2img-plan steps d fixed
    in let s = list-at p 0
    in i2-from (ti-sigmas (r.ti-sampler) (r.ti-scheduler) s sd15) (s - list-at p 1 - 1) []

 The whole schedule that tail is cut from, which Forge's Brownian tree spans.

  img2img-full-for : Txt2Img, Boolean, Integer, Real, Boolean -> List Real
  img2img-full-for (r) (sd15) (steps) (d) (fixed) = ti-sigmas (r.ti-sampler) (r.ti-scheduler) (list-at (img2img-plan steps d fixed) 0) sd15

Section: The Picture

 A staged file under -gpu-files read whole into guest memory, or 0.

  i2-read-file : Text, Integer -> Integer
  i2-read-file (name) (n) =
    let h = gpu-buf-alloc n
    in let a = alloc-bytes n
    in let ok = if h == 0 then False else gpu-buf-upload h 0 name 0 n gpu-dt-u8 gpu-dt-u8 == n & gpu-buf-read h 0 n a
    in let f = if h == 0 then True else gpu-buf-free h
    in if ok then a else 0

 Pillow's BLEND of two bytes under a mask byte.

  i2-blend8 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-blend8 (a) (b) (m) = let t = a * m + b * (255 - m) + 128 in bit-shru (t + bit-shru t 8) 8

  i2-rgb : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-rgb (px) (p) (c) = i2-blend8 (peek-byte px (p * 4 + c)) 255 (peek-byte px (p * 4 + 3))

  i2-rgb-bytes : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-rgb-bytes (px) (dst) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then dst
    else let w = poke-byte dst i (i2-rgb px (i / 3) (i - i / 3 * 3))
    in i2-rgb-bytes px dst (i + 1) n

  i2-row : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-row (rgb) (w) (y) (c) (x) (dst) =
    if x >= w then 0
    else let s = i2-set dst x (real-from-int (peek-byte rgb ((y * w + x) * 3 + c)) * 2.0 / 255.0 - 1.0)
    in i2-row rgb w y c (x + 1) dst

  i2-upload-rows : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  i2-upload-rows (rgb) (h) (w) (dev) (k) (row) =
    if k >= 3 * h then True
    else let c = k / h
    in let r = i2-row rgb w (k - c * h) c 0 row
    in if gpu-buf-write dev (k * w * 4) (w * 4) row == False then False
    else i2-upload-rows rgb h w dev (k + 1) row

 The flattened picture as 3 x h x w f32 in [-1, 1] on the device.

  img2img-picture : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Act
  img2img-picture (rgb) (h) (w) =
    let dev = gpu-buf-alloc (3 * h * w * 4)
    in let ok = if dev == 0 then False else i2-upload-rows rgb h w dev 0 (alloc-bytes (w * 4))
    in vd-act dev 3 h w ok

Section: Posterior

 The VAE's scaling factor: SDXL's 0.13025, SD1.5's 0.18215 (Forge's
 latent.py, SDXL and SD15).

  i2-latent-scale : Boolean -> Real
  i2-latent-scale (sd15) = if sd15 then 0.18215 else 0.13025

  img2img-posterior : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Real, Integer -> Integer
  img2img-posterior (mom) (eps) (out) (hw) (scale) (i) =
    if i >= 4 * hw then 0
    else let lv0 = i2-get mom (i + 4 * hw)
    in let lv = if lv0 < 0.0 - 30.0 then 0.0 - 30.0 else if lv0 > 20.0 then 20.0 else lv0
    in let s = i2-set out i ((i2-get mom i + sm-exp (0.5 * lv) * i2-get eps i) * scale)
    in img2img-posterior mom eps out hw scale (i + 1)

Section: Mask

  i2-luma : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-luma (px) (p) = bit-shru (peek-byte px (p * 4) * 19595 + peek-byte px (p * 4 + 1) * 38470 + peek-byte px (p * 4 + 2) * 7471 + 32768) 16

  i2-opaque : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  i2-opaque (px) (p) (n) = if p >= n then True else if peek-byte px (p * 4 + 3) /= 255 then False else i2-opaque px (p + 1) n

  i2-mask-l : Integer, Integer, Integer, Boolean, Integer -> Integer
  i2-mask-l (px) (dst) (n) (alpha) (p) =
    if p >= n then dst
    else let w = poke-byte dst p (if alpha then (if peek-byte px (p * 4 + 3) > 128 then 255 else 0) else i2-luma px p)
    in i2-mask-l px dst n alpha (p + 1)

  img2img-binary-mask : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  img2img-binary-mask (px) (n) = i2-mask-l px (alloc-bytes n) n (i2-opaque px 0 n == False) 0

 Soft inpainting's create_binary_mask (round=False): the alpha as it stands.

  img2img-soft-mask : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  img2img-soft-mask (px) (n) = i2-mask-soft px (alloc-bytes n) n (i2-opaque px 0 n == False) 0

  i2-mask-soft : Integer, Integer, Integer, Boolean, Integer -> Integer
  i2-mask-soft (px) (dst) (n) (alpha) (p) =
    if p >= n then dst
    else let w = poke-byte dst p (if alpha then peek-byte px (p * 4 + 3) else i2-luma px p)
    in i2-mask-soft px dst n alpha (p + 1)

  i2-gauss-raw : Integer, Real, Integer, List Real -> List Real
  i2-gauss-raw (k) (s) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= k then acc
    else let x = real-from-int (i - (k - 1) / 2)
    in i2-gauss-raw k s (i + 1) (list-push acc (sm-exp (0.0 - x * x / (2.0 * s * s))))

  i2-sum : List Real, Integer, Real -> Real
  i2-sum (xs) (i) (acc) = if i >= list-length xs then acc else i2-sum xs (i + 1) (acc + list-at xs i)

  i2-scale : List Real, Real, Integer, List Real -> List Real
  i2-scale (xs) (k) (i) (acc) = if i >= list-length xs then acc else i2-scale xs k (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at xs i * k))

  i2-gauss : Integer -> List Real
  i2-gauss (blur) =
    let raw = i2-gauss-raw (2 * real-to-int (2.5 * real-from-int blur + 0.5) + 1) (real-from-int blur) 0 []
    in i2-scale raw (1.0 / i2-sum raw 0 0.0) 0 []

  i2-reflect : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-reflect (i) (n) =
    if n == 1 then 0
    else if i < 0 then i2-reflect (0 - i) n
    else if i >= n then i2-reflect (2 * n - 2 - i) n
    else i

  i2-tap : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Boolean, List Real, Integer, Real -> Real
  i2-tap (src) (w) (h) (p) (across) (k) (j) (acc) =
    if j >= list-length k then acc
    else let r = (list-length k - 1) / 2
    in let y = p / w
    in let x = p - y * w
    in let q = if across then y * w + i2-reflect (x + j - r) w else i2-reflect (y + j - r) h * w + x
    in i2-tap src w h p across k (j + 1) (acc + list-at k j * real-from-int (peek-byte src q))

  i2-blur-pass : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Boolean, List Real, Integer -> Integer
  i2-blur-pass (src) (dst) (w) (h) (across) (k) (p) =
    if p >= w * h then dst
    else let v = real-to-int (i2-tap src w h p across k 0 0.0 + 0.5)
    in let s = poke-byte dst p (if v > 255 then 255 else if v < 0 then 0 else v)
    in i2-blur-pass src dst w h across k (p + 1)

  img2img-blur : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  img2img-blur (m) (w) (h) (blur) =
    if blur <= 0 then m
    else let k = i2-gauss blur
    in let a = i2-blur-pass m (alloc-bytes (w * h)) w h True k 0
    in i2-blur-pass a (alloc-bytes (w * h)) w h False k 0

  i2-double : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-double (m) (dst) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then dst
    else let v = 2 * peek-byte m i
    in let s = poke-byte dst i (if v > 255 then 255 else v)
    in i2-double m dst (i + 1) n

  img2img-overlay-mask : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  img2img-overlay-mask (m) (n) = i2-double m (alloc-bytes n) 0 n

 Pillow's bicubic reduction along one axis.

  i2-cubic : Real -> Real
  i2-cubic (x0) =
    let x = i2-abs x0
    in if x < 1.0 then (1.5 * x - 2.5) * x * x + 1.0
    else if x < 2.0 then (((x - 5.0) * x + 8.0) * x - 4.0) * (0.0 - 0.5)
    else 0.0

  i2-weights : Integer, Real, Real, Real, Integer, List Real -> List Real
  i2-weights (xmin) (center) (fs) (x) (n) (acc) =
    if real-to-int x >= n then acc
    else i2-weights xmin center fs (x + 1.0) n (list-push acc (i2-cubic ((x + real-from-int xmin - center + 0.5) / fs)))

  i2-fixed : List Real, Real, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  i2-fixed (ws) (total) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length ws then acc
    else let k = (if total ~0 0.0 then list-at ws i else list-at ws i / total) * 4194304.0
    in i2-fixed ws total (i + 1) (list-push acc (if k < 0.0 then real-to-int (k - 0.5) else real-to-int (k + 0.5)))

  I2Coeffs = record {
    ic-min : Integer,
    ic-k : List Integer
  }

  i2-coeffs : Integer, Integer, Integer -> I2Coeffs
  i2-coeffs (inn) (outn) (xx) =
    let scale = real-from-int inn / real-from-int outn
    in let fs = if scale < 1.0 then 1.0 else scale
    in let support = 2.0 * fs
    in let center = (real-from-int xx + 0.5) * scale
    in let lo0 = real-to-int (center - support + 0.5)
    in let lo = if lo0 < 0 then 0 else lo0
    in let hi0 = real-to-int (center + support + 0.5)
    in let hi = if hi0 > inn then inn else hi0
    in let ws = i2-weights lo center fs 0.0 (hi - lo) []
    in I2Coeffs { ic-min = lo, ic-k = i2-fixed ws (i2-sum ws 0 0.0) 0 [] }

  i2-dot8 : Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-dot8 (src) (base) (stride) (k) (j) (acc) =
    if j >= list-length k then acc
    else i2-dot8 src base stride k (j + 1) (acc + peek-byte src (base + j * stride) * list-at k j)

  i2-clip8 : Integer -> Integer
  i2-clip8 (v) = let s = bit-shr v 22 in if s < 0 then 0 else if s > 255 then 255 else s

  i2-resize-h : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List I2Coeffs, Integer -> Integer
  i2-resize-h (src) (dst) (w) (h) (ow) (cs) (p) =
    if p >= h * ow then dst
    else let y = p / ow
    in let c = list-at cs (p - y * ow)
    in let s = poke-byte dst p (i2-clip8 (2097152 + i2-dot8 src (y * w + c.ic-min) 1 (c.ic-k) 0 0))
    in i2-resize-h src dst w h ow cs (p + 1)

  i2-resize-v : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List I2Coeffs, Integer -> Integer
  i2-resize-v (src) (dst) (w) (oh) (cs) (p) =
    if p >= oh * w then dst
    else let y = p / w
    in let c = list-at cs y
    in let s = poke-byte dst p (i2-clip8 (2097152 + i2-dot8 src (c.ic-min * w + p - y * w) w (c.ic-k) 0 0))
    in i2-resize-v src dst w oh cs (p + 1)

  i2-all-coeffs : Integer, Integer, Integer, List I2Coeffs -> List I2Coeffs
  i2-all-coeffs (inn) (outn) (i) (acc) = if i >= outn then acc else i2-all-coeffs inn outn (i + 1) (list-push acc (i2-coeffs inn outn i))

  img2img-reduce : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  img2img-reduce (m) (w) (h) (ow) (oh) =
    let a = i2-resize-h m (alloc-bytes (h * ow)) w h ow (i2-all-coeffs w ow 0 []) 0
    in i2-resize-v a (alloc-bytes (oh * ow)) ow oh (i2-all-coeffs h oh 0 []) 0

 The latent mask: 1 where the reduced mask is at least 128, one byte per
 latent pixel.

  i2-round : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-round (m) (dst) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then dst
    else let s = poke-byte dst i (if peek-byte m i >= 128 then 1 else 0)
    in i2-round m dst (i + 1) n

  img2img-latent-mask : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  img2img-latent-mask (blurred) (w) (h) = i2-round (img2img-reduce blurred w h (w / 8) (h / 8)) (alloc-bytes (w / 8 * (h / 8))) 0 (w / 8 * (h / 8))

 Pillow's alpha_composite of an overlay pixel of alpha a over an opaque one,
 the overlay being the original premultiplied by a then unpremultiplied.

  i2-over : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-over (orig) (a) (gen) =
    if a == 0 then gen
    else let pm = i2-blend8 orig 0 a
    in let src0 = if a == 255 then pm else (255 * pm) / a
    in let src = if src0 > 255 then 255 else src0
    in let t = (src * a + gen * (255 - a)) * 128 + 16384
    in bit-shru (bit-shru t 8 + t) 8 / 128

  img2img-composite : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  img2img-composite (rgb) (mfo) (gen) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then gen
    else let s = poke-byte gen i (i2-over (peek-byte rgb i) (255 - peek-byte mfo (i / 3)) (peek-byte gen i))
    in img2img-composite rgb mfo gen (i + 1) n

Section: Masked Content

 Forge's latent nothing (3) and latent noise (2) on the init latent before
 sampling (processing.py:1834-1840): times 1 - the latent mask, plus, for
 latent noise, the mask times create_random_tensors of the seed alone, a
 fresh generator's first draw with no variation.

  i2-content : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-content (init) (nz) (lm) (hw) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then 0
    else let m = real-from-int (peek-byte lm (i - i / hw * hw))
    in let k = i2-get init i * (1.0 - m)
    in let s = i2-set init i (if nz == 0 then k else k + i2-get nz i * m)
    in i2-content init nz lm hw (i + 1) n

  img2img-content : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  img2img-content (fill) (init) (lm) (hw) (seed) =
    let n = 4 * hw
    in if fill == 3 then i2-content init 0 lm hw 0 n
    else if fill == 2 then (let nz = alloc-bytes (n * 4) in let z = noise-torch-into nz seed 0 n in i2-content init nz lm hw 0 n)
    else 0

  i2-soft-content : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-soft-content (fill) (init) (nm) (hw) (seed) =
    if fill == 3 then soft-content 3 init 0 nm hw
    else if fill == 2 then (let nz = alloc-bytes (4 * hw * 4) in let z = noise-torch-into nz seed 0 (4 * hw) in soft-content 2 init nz nm hw)
    else 0

Section: Latent Resize

  i2-src : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Real
  i2-src (o) (inn) (outn) =
    let s = (real-from-int o + 0.5) * (real-from-int inn / real-from-int outn) - 0.5
    in if s < 0.0 then 0.0 else s

  i2-bilinear-at : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Real
  i2-bilinear-at (src) (h) (w) (oh) (ow) (i) =
    let c = i / (oh * ow)
    in let r = i - c * oh * ow
    in let oy = r / ow
    in let sy = i2-src oy h oh
    in let sx = i2-src (r - oy * ow) w ow
    in let y0 = real-to-int sy
    in let x0 = real-to-int sx
    in let y1 = if y0 < h - 1 then y0 + 1 else y0
    in let x1 = if x0 < w - 1 then x0 + 1 else x0
    in let ly = sy - real-from-int y0
    in let lx = sx - real-from-int x0
    in let base = c * h * w
    in (1.0 - ly) * ((1.0 - lx) * i2-get src (base + y0 * w + x0) + lx * i2-get src (base + y0 * w + x1)) + ly * ((1.0 - lx) * i2-get src (base + y1 * w + x0) + lx * i2-get src (base + y1 * w + x1))

  img2img-bilinear : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  img2img-bilinear (src) (dst) (h) (w) (oh) (ow) (i) =
    if i >= 4 * oh * ow then dst
    else let s = i2-set dst i (i2-bilinear-at src h w oh ow i)
    in img2img-bilinear src dst h w oh ow (i + 1)

Section: Masked Denoiser

  I2Mask = record {
    mk-latent : Integer,
    mk-init : Integer,
    mk-hw : Integer,
    mk-gx : Integer,
    mk-gn : Integer,
    mk-dev : Integer
  }

  i2-keep : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Real, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-keep (x) (init) (nz) (lm) (hw) (s) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then 0
    else let w = if peek-byte lm (i - i / hw * hw) == 1 then 0 else i2-set x i (i2-get init i + i2-get nz i * s)
    in i2-keep x init nz lm hw s (i + 1) n

  i2-settle : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-settle (x) (init) (lm) (hw) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then 0
    else let w = if peek-byte lm (i - i / hw * hw) == 1 then 0 else poke-32 x (i * 4) (peek-32 init (i * 4))
    in i2-settle x init lm hw (i + 1) n

 The kept region of a device latent set to the init latent.

  img2img-settle : I2Mask, Integer -> Boolean
  img2img-settle (m) (x) =
    let n = 4 * m.mk-hw
    in if gpu-buf-read x 0 (n * 4) (m.mk-gx) == False then False
    else let s = i2-settle (m.mk-gx) (m.mk-init) (m.mk-latent) (m.mk-hw) 0 n
    in gpu-buf-write x 0 (n * 4) (m.mk-gx)

 One model call under soft inpainting, mk-latent the unrounded mask.

  img2img-soft-masked : I2Mask, SoftCfg, Integer, (Integer, Real -> Integer), (Real -> Integer), Integer, Real -> Integer
  img2img-soft-masked (m) (sc) (tb) (den) (noise) (x) (s) =
    let n = 4 * m.mk-hw
    in let nb = noise s
    in let ok = nb /= 0 & gpu-buf-read x 0 (n * 4) (m.mk-gx) & gpu-buf-read nb 0 (n * 4) (m.mk-gn)
    in let k = if ok then soft-keep (m.mk-gx) (m.mk-init) (m.mk-gn) (m.mk-latent) (m.mk-hw) s 0 else 0
    in if ok == False | gpu-buf-write (m.mk-dev) 0 (n * 4) (m.mk-gx) == False then 0
    else let d = den (m.mk-dev) s
    in if d == 0 | gpu-buf-read d 0 (n * 4) (m.mk-gn) == False then 0
    else let t = soft-modified sc (m.mk-latent) tb (m.mk-hw) s
    in let b = soft-latent-blend sc (m.mk-init) (m.mk-gn) t (m.mk-gn) (m.mk-hw)
    in if gpu-buf-write d 0 (n * 4) (m.mk-gn) then d
    else let f = gpu-buf-free d in 0

 One model call under the mask: noise answers the device buffer of the
 call's draw.

  img2img-masked : I2Mask, (Integer, Real -> Integer), (Real -> Integer), Integer, Real -> Integer
  img2img-masked (m) (den) (noise) (x) (s) =
    let n = 4 * m.mk-hw
    in let nb = noise s
    in let ok = nb /= 0 & gpu-buf-read x 0 (n * 4) (m.mk-gx) & gpu-buf-read nb 0 (n * 4) (m.mk-gn)
    in let k = if ok then i2-keep (m.mk-gx) (m.mk-init) (m.mk-gn) (m.mk-latent) (m.mk-hw) s 0 n else 0
    in if ok == False | gpu-buf-write (m.mk-dev) 0 (n * 4) (m.mk-gx) == False then 0
    else let d = den (m.mk-dev) s
    in if d == 0 then 0
    else if img2img-settle m d then d
    else let f = gpu-buf-free d in 0

Section: Generation

  i2-torch-seed : Integer -> Integer
  i2-torch-seed (seed) = let v = seed + 100000 in v - v / 65536 * 65536

 The next draw of the global CUDA generator into buffer nb; drawn holds how
 many it has given.

  i2-blend : Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> Integer
  i2-blend (nb) (seed) (n) (drawn) =
    let k = list-at drawn 0
    in let c = list-set-at drawn 0 (k + 1)
    in if noise-torch nb (i2-torch-seed seed) k n then nb else 0

  i2-den : TiCfg, Integer, Real -> Integer
  i2-den (c) (x) (s) =
    if c.tc-cfg ~0 1.0 then (let tick = ti-tick (c.tc-extras) in i2-den-one c (ti-model c (c.tc-yc) (c.tc-cc) x s) x s)
    else ti-den c x s

 Forge skips the uncond call at guidance 1 and still runs its post-CFG
 functions on the cond prediction.

 Dynamic thresholding at guidance 1 takes the uncond prediction as zero,
 which is what Forge's skipped uncond call leaves.

  i2-dt-one : TiCfg, Integer, Real -> Integer
  i2-dt-one (c) (dc) (s) =
    let n = 4 * c.tc-h * c.tc-w
    in let z = gpu-buf-alloc (n * 4)
    in let o = gpu-buf-alloc (n * 4)
    in let r = if z == 0 | o == 0 then 0 - 1 else if sm-lincomb dc dc dc z 0.0 0.0 0.0 n < 0 then 0 - 1 else ti-combine c s dc z o n
    in let f = un-free 0 z
    in if r < 0 then un-free 0 o else o

  i2-den-one : TiCfg, Integer, Integer, Real -> Integer
  i2-den-one (c) (dc) (x) (s) =
    let g = if dc == 0 | list-length ((c.tc-extras).tx-dt) == 0 then dc else i2-dt-one c dc s
    in let o = if g == 0 then 0 else ti-post c x s dc 0 0 g
    in if o /= dc & dc /= 0 then un-free o dc else o

  i2-sample : Txt2Img, TiCfg, Integer, List Real, List Real, Integer, (Integer, Real -> Integer) -> Integer
 Over a schedule's tail, DPM fast and DPM adaptive run from its first sigma
 to its next-to-last, DPM fast in one evaluation per step (Forge's
 sample_img2img).

  i2-sample (r) (tc) (x) (sig) (full) (n) (den) = i2-sample-with r (\k -> tc) x sig full n den

  i2-sample-with : Txt2Img, (Integer -> TiCfg), Integer, List Real, List Real, Integer, (Integer, Real -> Integer) -> Integer
  i2-sample-with (r) (cur) (x) (sig) (full) (n) (den) =
    let nb = gpu-buf-alloc (n * 4)
    in let len = list-length sig
    in let l = ti-launch ((cur 0).tc-extras) (r.ti-sampler) (len - 1)
    in let bad = if nb == 0 | len < 2 then 1 else ti-sample-with (r.ti-sampler) den (\xh s ub -> ti-den3 (cur 0) xh s ub) x sig full (len - 1) (list-at sig (len - 2)) (list-at sig 0) (len - 1) n nb (r.ti-seed)
    in let f = if nb == 0 then True else gpu-buf-free nb
    in bad

  I2Start = record {
    is-x : Integer,
    is-rgb : Integer,
    is-mfo : Integer,
    is-why : Text
  }

  i2-fail : Text -> I2Start
  i2-fail (why) = I2Start { is-x = 0, is-rgb = 0, is-mfo = 0, is-why = why }

 A checkpoint's weights, loaded once and kept on the device while requests
 name it. The family is SDXL when every SDXL tensor binds, else SD1.5 when
 every SD1.5 tensor binds; SD1.5 has no OpenCLIP-G.

  I2Model = record {
    im-ckpt : Text,
    im-why : Text,
    im-sd15 : Boolean,
    im-wl : ClipWeights,
    im-wg : ClipWeights,
    im-unet : UNetFile,
    im-tab : List Real,
    im-vd : VaeWeights,
    im-ve : VaeWeights
  }

  i2-no-clip : ClipSpec -> ClipWeights
  i2-no-clip (s) = ClipWeights { cw-spec = s, cw-status = 0 - 1, cw-path = "", cw-tok = BoundTensor { bt-name = "", bt-dtype = 0, bt-shape = [], bt-offset = 0, bt-bytes = 0 }, cw-pos = 0, cw-layers = [], cw-final-g = 0, cw-final-b = 0, cw-proj = 0 }

  img2img-model : Text -> I2Model
  img2img-model (ckpt) =
    let file = ckpt-open ckpt
    in let lx = layout-bind file sdxl-layout
    in let xl = file.st-valid & parts-complete (lx.lb-parts) 0
    in let l15 = if xl then lx else layout-bind file sd15-layout
    in let sd15 = xl == False & file.st-valid & parts-complete (l15.lb-parts) 0
    in let ok = xl | sd15
    in let lb = if sd15 then l15 else lx
    in let vpart = if ok then ti-vae-part (lb.lb-parts) 0 else PartBinding { pb-name = "vae", pb-required = 0, pb-bound = [], pb-missing = [], pb-misshapen = [], pb-optional = 0 }
    in let wl = if ok then clip-load ckpt file lb (if sd15 then clip-l15-spec else clip-l-spec) else i2-no-clip clip-l-spec
    in let wg = if xl then clip-load ckpt file lb openclip-g-spec else i2-no-clip openclip-g-spec
    in I2Model { im-ckpt = ckpt, im-why = (if ok then "" else "refused: " & ckpt & " is not a readable SDXL or SD1.5 checkpoint"), im-sd15 = sd15, im-wl = wl, im-wg = wg, im-unet = (if ok then unet-load (unet-open ckpt) else unet-open ckpt), im-tab = unet-log-sigmas 0, im-vd = vae-load ckpt vpart "first_stage_model.", im-ve = vae-encoder-load ckpt vpart "first_stage_model." }

  i2-skip : I2Model, Integer -> I2Model
  i2-skip (m) (k) = I2Model { im-ckpt = m.im-ckpt, im-why = m.im-why, im-sd15 = m.im-sd15, im-wl = ce-skip (m.im-wl) k, im-wg = ce-skip (m.im-wg) k, im-unet = m.im-unet, im-tab = m.im-tab, im-vd = m.im-vd, im-ve = m.im-ve }

  i2-layer-handles : List ClipLayer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  i2-layer-handles (ys) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length ys then acc
    else let y = list-at ys i
    in i2-layer-handles ys (i + 1) (acc & [y.cy-ln1-g, y.cy-ln1-b, y.cy-q-w, y.cy-q-b, y.cy-k-w, y.cy-k-b, y.cy-v-w, y.cy-v-b, y.cy-o-w, y.cy-o-b, y.cy-ln2-g, y.cy-ln2-b, y.cy-fc1-w, y.cy-fc1-b, y.cy-fc2-w, y.cy-fc2-b])

  i2-clip-free : ClipWeights -> Integer
  i2-clip-free (w) = ce-free-all ([w.cw-pos, w.cw-final-g, w.cw-final-b, w.cw-proj] & i2-layer-handles (w.cw-layers) 0 []) 0

  img2img-model-free : I2Model -> Integer
  img2img-model-free (m) = ti-free-all ((m.im-unet).uf-handles) 0 0 + i2-clip-free (m.im-wl) + i2-clip-free (m.im-wg) + vae-free (m.im-vd) 0 0 + vae-free (m.im-ve) 0 0

 img2img or inpaint from the staged picture: the init latent, the start and
 the sampling, with the mask blended where there is one.

  i2-from-picture : I2i, TiCfg, I2Model, (Integer -> TiCfg) -> I2Start
  i2-from-picture (q) (tc) (m) (cur) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let h = r.ti-height
    in let w = r.ti-width
    in let sw = if q.i2-src-w > 0 then q.i2-src-w else w
    in let sh = if q.i2-src-h > 0 then q.i2-src-h else h
    in let px = i2-read-file (q.i2-image) (sw * sh * 4)
    in if px == 0 then i2-fail "refused: the picture could not be read"
    else let src = i2-rgb-bytes px (alloc-bytes (sw * sh * 3)) 0 (sw * sh * 3)
    in let only = q.i2-area == 1 & q.i2-mask /= ""
    in let m0 = if only then i2-mask-blurred q sw sh sw sh else 0
    in let box = if m0 == 0 then [] else i2-box q m0 sw sh w h
    in if only & m0 == 0 then i2-fail "refused: the mask could not be read"
    else if list-length box > 0 then i2-only-masked q tc m src sw sh m0 box cur
    else let rgb = if (sw == w & sh == h) | q.i2-resize == 3 then src else resize-mode (q.i2-resize) src sw sh w h
    in if rgb == 0 then i2-fail ("refused: resize mode " & show (q.i2-resize) & " is not built")
    else let blurred = if q.i2-mask == "" | only then 0 else i2-mask-blurred q w h sw sh
    in if q.i2-mask /= "" & only == False & blurred == 0 then i2-fail "refused: the mask could not be read"
    else let pic = img2img-picture (if q.i2-fill == 0 & blurred /= 0 then inpaint-fill rgb blurred w h else rgb) (if q.i2-resize == 3 then sh else h) (if q.i2-resize == 3 then sw else w)
    in let mom = if pic.ah == 0 then pic else vae-encode (m.im-ve) pic
    in let f2 = vd-free pic
    in if mom.ah == 0 then i2-fail "encode failed"
    else i2-with-moments q tc rgb mom blurred (if blurred == 0 then 0 else img2img-overlay-mask blurred (w * h)) cur

 Only masked (Diffusion chapter InpaintMasked): an empty box is a blank mask,
 which Forge runs as img2img with no mask.

  i2-box : I2i, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  i2-box (q) (m0) (sw) (sh) (w) (h) =
    let b = inpaint-crop-box m0 sw sh (q.i2-padding)
    in if list-length b == 0 then [] else inpaint-expand-box b w h sw sh

  i2-only-masked : I2i, TiCfg, I2Model, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer, (Integer -> TiCfg) -> I2Start
  i2-only-masked (q) (tc) (m) (src) (sw) (sh) (m0) (box) (cur) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let h = r.ti-height
    in let w = r.ti-width
    in let crop = inpaint-crop-rgb src sw box w h
    in let lmask = inpaint-crop-l m0 sw box w h
    in let pic = img2img-picture (if q.i2-fill == 0 then inpaint-fill crop lmask w h else crop) h w
    in let mom = if pic.ah == 0 then pic else vae-encode (m.im-ve) pic
    in let f2 = vd-free pic
    in if mom.ah == 0 then i2-fail "encode failed"
    else let st = i2-with-moments q tc src mom lmask m0 cur
    in if q.i2-soft == 1 & st.is-x /= 0 then I2Start { is-x = st.is-x, is-rgb = st.is-rgb, is-mfo = i2-uncrop-l (st.is-mfo) w h box sw sh, is-why = "" } else st

 uncrop of the soft overlay mask: resized into the box of a picture-sized
 canvas that is black outside it (processing.py uncrop, an RGBA canvas read
 as L).

  i2-uncrop-l : Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-uncrop-l (m) (pw) (ph) (b) (sw) (sh) =
    let cw = list-at b 2 - list-at b 0
    in let ch = list-at b 3 - list-at b 1
    in let placed = im-place (i2-zero-bytes (alloc-bytes (sw * sh * 3 + 8)) 0 (sw * sh * 3)) sw (resize-mode 1 (si-grey3 m (alloc-bytes (pw * ph * 3)) 0 (pw * ph)) pw ph cw ch) b 0 (cw * ch * 3)
    in si-band0 placed (alloc-bytes (sw * sh)) 0 (sw * sh)

  i2-mask-blurred : I2i, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-mask-blurred (q) (w) (h) (sw) (sh) =
    let px = i2-read-file (q.i2-mask) (sw * sh * 4)
    in if px == 0 then 0
    else let b = img2img-blur (if q.i2-soft == 1 then img2img-soft-mask px (sw * sh) else img2img-binary-mask px (sw * sh)) sw sh (q.i2-blur)
    in if sw == w & sh == h then b else resize-mode-l (q.i2-resize) b sw sh w h

  i2-with-moments : I2i, TiCfg, Integer, Act, Integer, Integer, (Integer -> TiCfg) -> I2Start
  i2-with-moments (q) (tc) (rgb) (mom) (blurred) (mfo) (cur) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let shw = mom.ahh * mom.aww
    in let th = r.ti-height / 8
    in let tw = r.ti-width / 8
    in let hw = th * tw
    in let n = 4 * hw
    in let gm = alloc-bytes (8 * shw * 4)
    in let ge = alloc-bytes (4 * shw * 4)
    in let post = alloc-bytes (4 * shw * 4)
    in let x = gpu-buf-alloc (n * 4)
    in let nb = gpu-buf-alloc (n * 4)
    in let ok = x /= 0 & nb /= 0 & gpu-buf-read (mom.ah) 0 (8 * shw * 4) gm & noise-torch-cpu-into ge (i2-torch-seed (if q.i2-post >= 0 then q.i2-post else r.ti-seed)) (4 * shw) == 0
    in let p = if ok then img2img-posterior gm ge post shw (i2-latent-scale (tc.tc-sd15)) 0 else 0
    in let init = if shw == hw then post else img2img-bilinear post (alloc-bytes (n * 4)) (mom.ahh) (mom.aww) th tw 0
    in let f = vd-free mom
    in let lm = if blurred == 0 then 0 else if q.i2-soft == 1 then soft-nmask (img2img-reduce blurred (r.ti-width) (r.ti-height) tw th) hw else img2img-latent-mask blurred (r.ti-width) (r.ti-height)
    in let c = if ok == False | lm == 0 then 0 else if q.i2-soft == 1 then i2-soft-content (q.i2-fill) init lm hw (r.ti-seed) else img2img-content (q.i2-fill) init lm hw (r.ti-seed)
    in let sig = img2img-sigmas-for r (tc.tc-sd15) (r.ti-steps) (q.i2-denoise) False
    in if ok == False | gpu-buf-write x 0 (n * 4) init == False | va-noise nb (r.ti-seed) (q.i2-var) 4 th tw == False then i2-fail "the init latent could not be staged"
    else let s0 = sm-lincomb x nb nb x 1.0 (list-at sig 0) 0.0 n
    in let fb = gpu-buf-free nb
    in if lm == 0 then i2-run q tc x sig n init 0 rgb 0 cur
    else i2-run q tc x sig n init lm rgb mfo cur

  i2-run : I2i, TiCfg, Integer, List Real, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, (Integer -> TiCfg) -> I2Start
  i2-run (q) (tc) (x) (sig) (n) (init) (lm) (rgb) (mfo) (cur) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let mk = I2Mask { mk-latent = lm, mk-init = init, mk-hw = n / 4, mk-gx = alloc-bytes (n * 4), mk-gn = alloc-bytes (n * 4), mk-dev = gpu-buf-alloc (n * 4) }
    in let nb = gpu-buf-alloc (n * 4)
    in let drawn = [0]
    in let noise = \s -> i2-blend nb (r.ti-seed) n drawn
    in let soft = lm /= 0 & q.i2-soft == 1
    in let tb = if soft then alloc-bytes (n / 4 * 4) else 0
    in let den = if lm == 0 then (\xh s -> ti-den (cur 0) xh s) else if soft then (\xh s -> img2img-soft-masked mk (q.i2-sc) tb (\xx ss -> ti-den (cur 0) xx ss) noise xh s) else (\xh s -> img2img-masked mk (\xx ss -> ti-den (cur 0) xx ss) noise xh s)
    in let bad = i2-sample-with r cur x sig (img2img-full-for r (tc.tc-sd15) (r.ti-steps) (q.i2-denoise) False) n den
    in let settled = if lm == 0 | soft then True else img2img-settle mk x
    in let f = gpu-buf-free nb & gpu-buf-free (mk.mk-dev)
    in let smask = if soft & bad == 0 & gpu-buf-read x 0 (n * 4) (mk.mk-gx) then soft-adaptive-mask (q.i2-sc) (mk.mk-gx) init lm (r.ti-width / 8) (r.ti-height / 8) (r.ti-width) (r.ti-height) else 0
    in if bad > 0 | settled == False | (soft & smask == 0) then i2-fail ("sampling failed: " & show bad & " refused steps")
    else I2Start { is-x = x, is-rgb = (if lm == 0 then 0 else rgb), is-mfo = (if soft then smask else mfo), is-why = "" }

 txt2img at the base size, as Txt2Img's ti-sample does.

  i2-plain : I2i, TiCfg -> I2Start
  i2-plain (q) (tc) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let n = 4 * tc.tc-h * tc.tc-w
    in let x = gpu-buf-alloc (n * 4)
    in let ok = x /= 0 & va-noise x (r.ti-seed) (q.i2-var) 4 (tc.tc-h) (tc.tc-w)
    in let bad = if ok == False then 1 else ti-txt2img-run r tc x n
    in if bad > 0 then i2-fail ("sampling failed: " & show bad & " refused steps")
    else I2Start { is-x = x, is-rgb = 0, is-mfo = 0, is-why = "" }

 The hires pass on the resized latent of i2-plain's.

  i2-hires : I2i, TiCfg, TiCfg -> I2Start
  i2-hires (q) (tc) (hc) =
    let first = i2-first-latent q tc (hc.tc-h) (hc.tc-w)
    in if first.is-rgb == 0 then first
    else i2-hires-latent q hc (first.is-rgb) (\k -> hc)

  i2-first-latent : I2i, TiCfg, Integer, Integer -> I2Start
  i2-first-latent (q) (tc) (hh) (hw) =
    let first = i2-plain q tc
    in if first.is-x == 0 then first
    else let x = first.is-x
    in let n = 4 * tc.tc-h * tc.tc-w
    in let gx = alloc-bytes (n * 4)
    in let gy = alloc-bytes (4 * hh * hw * 4)
    in let up = gpu-buf-read x 0 (n * 4) gx
    in let rs = if up then img2img-bilinear gx gy (tc.tc-h) (tc.tc-w) hh hw 0 else 0
    in let f = gpu-buf-free x
    in if up == False then i2-fail "the first pass could not be read" else I2Start { is-x = 0, is-rgb = gy, is-mfo = 0, is-why = "" }

  i2-hires-latent : I2i, TiCfg, Integer, (Integer -> TiCfg) -> I2Start
  i2-hires-latent (q) (hc) (gy) (cur) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let n2 = 4 * hc.tc-h * hc.tc-w
    in let x2 = gpu-buf-alloc (n2 * 4)
    in let nb = gpu-buf-alloc (n2 * 4)
    in let steps = if q.i2-hr-steps > 0 then q.i2-hr-steps else r.ti-steps
    in let hsig = img2img-sigmas-for (i2-hr-base q) (hc.tc-sd15) steps (q.i2-hr-denoise) True
    in if x2 == 0 | nb == 0 | gpu-buf-write x2 0 (n2 * 4) gy == False | va-noise nb (r.ti-seed) (q.i2-var) 4 (hc.tc-h) (hc.tc-w) == False then i2-fail "the hires latent could not be staged"
    else let s1 = sm-lincomb x2 nb nb x2 1.0 (list-at hsig 0) 0.0 n2
    in let fb = gpu-buf-free nb
    in let bad2 = i2-sample-with (i2-hr-base q) cur x2 hsig (img2img-full-for (i2-hr-base q) (hc.tc-sd15) steps (q.i2-hr-denoise) True) n2 (\xh s -> i2-den (cur 0) xh s)
    in if bad2 > 0 then i2-fail ("hires sampling failed: " & show bad2 & " refused steps")
    else I2Start { is-x = x2, is-rgb = 0, is-mfo = 0, is-why = "" }

 The hires pass through an upscaler, as sample_hr_pass's non-latent branch:
 the first pass decoded and truncated to bytes, 255 clamp ((x + 1) / 2) in
 f32 then astype (uint8); resize_image to the hires size, which for a scale
 above 1 runs Upscaler.upscale (the model once, then LANCZOS to (int (W
 scale) // 8 * 8, the same for H) when that differs) and then LANCZOS to the
 hires size when that differs; the picture encoded and started as img2img
 starts, over the hires schedule.

  i2-trunc-bytes : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-trunc-bytes (host) (hw) (dst) (i) =
    if i >= hw * 3 then dst
    else let c = i - i / 3 * 3
    in let v = sm-f32 (sm-f32 (esr-f32 (peek-32 host ((c * hw + i / 3) * 4)) + 1.0) / 2.0)
    in let k = if v < 0.0 then 0.0 else if v > 1.0 then 1.0 else v
    in let b = poke-byte dst i (real-to-int (sm-f32 (255.0 * k)))
    in i2-trunc-bytes host hw dst (i + 1)

  i2-upscaled : Text, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-upscaled (path) (rgb) (w) (h) (fw) (fh) =
    let sx = real-from-int fw / real-from-int w
    in let sy = real-from-int fh / real-from-int h
    in let scale = if sx > sy then sx else sy
    in if scale <= 1.0 then resize-lanczos rgb w h fw fh
    else let dw = 8 * real-to-int (real-from-int w * scale / 8.0)
    in let dh = 8 * real-to-int (real-from-int h * scale / 8.0)
    in let f = if w >= dw & h >= dh then pth-fail path "" else pth-open path
    in let swin = f.pf-ok & swin-is f
    in let dat = f.pf-ok & dat-is f
    in let wts = if swin | dat then esr-load (pth-fail path "") else esr-load f
    in let up = if w >= dw & h >= dh then rgb else if f.pf-ok == False then 0 else if swin then swin-upscale-file f rgb w h 192 8 else if dat then dat-upscale-file f rgb w h 192 8 else esr-upscale wts (esr-blocks f 0) rgb w h 192 8
    in let uw = if w >= dw & h >= dh then w else 4 * w
    in let uh = if w >= dw & h >= dh then h else 4 * h
    in let fr = vae-free wts 0 0
    in if up == 0 then 0
    else let d1 = if uw == dw & uh == dh then up else resize-lanczos up uw uh dw dh
    in if dw == fw & dh == fh then d1 else resize-lanczos d1 dw dh fw fh

  i2-hires-upscaled : I2i, TiCfg, TiCfg, I2Model -> I2Start
  i2-hires-upscaled (q) (tc) (hc) (m) =
    let first = i2-first-bytes q tc m
    in if first.is-rgb == 0 then first
    else i2-hires-picture q tc hc m (first.is-rgb) (\k -> hc)

  i2-first-bytes : I2i, TiCfg, I2Model -> I2Start
  i2-first-bytes (q) (tc) (m) =
    let first = i2-plain q tc
    in if first.is-x == 0 then first
    else let x = first.is-x
    in let hw = tc.tc-h * tc.tc-w * 64
    in let z = sm-lincomb x x x x (1.0 / i2-latent-scale (tc.tc-sd15)) 0.0 0.0 (4 * tc.tc-h * tc.tc-w)
    in let img = vae-decode (m.im-vd) (Act { ah = x, ac = 4, ahh = tc.tc-h, aww = tc.tc-w })
    in let fx = gpu-buf-free x
    in let host = alloc-bytes (3 * hw * 4)
    in let got = img.ah /= 0 & gpu-buf-read (img.ah) 0 (3 * hw * 4) host
    in let fi = vd-free img
    in if got == False then i2-fail "the first pass could not be decoded"
    else I2Start { is-x = 0, is-rgb = i2-trunc-bytes host hw (alloc-bytes (hw * 3)) 0, is-mfo = 0, is-why = "" }

  i2-hires-picture : I2i, TiCfg, TiCfg, I2Model, Integer, (Integer -> TiCfg) -> I2Start
  i2-hires-picture (q) (tc) (hc) (m) (bytes) (cur) =
    let fw = hc.tc-w * 8
    in let fh = hc.tc-h * 8
    in let up = i2-upscaled (q.i2-hr-upscaler) bytes (tc.tc-w * 8) (tc.tc-h * 8) fw fh
    in if up == 0 then i2-fail ("the upscaler did not run: " & q.i2-hr-upscaler)
    else let pic = img2img-picture up fh fw
    in let mom = if pic.ah == 0 then pic else vae-encode (m.im-ve) pic
    in let fp = vd-free pic
    in if mom.ah == 0 then i2-fail "encode failed"
    else i2-hires-from mom q hc cur

 The upscaled picture's moments to a sampled hires latent: the posterior draw
 as img2img's, the start noise the seed's draw 0 at the hires size (a new
 ImageRNG), the hires schedule, the hires model call.

  i2-hires-from : Act, I2i, TiCfg, (Integer -> TiCfg) -> I2Start
  i2-hires-from (mom) (q) (hc) (cur) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let hw = mom.ahh * mom.aww
    in let n = 4 * hw
    in let gm = alloc-bytes (8 * hw * 4)
    in let ge = alloc-bytes (n * 4)
    in let init = alloc-bytes (n * 4)
    in let x2 = gpu-buf-alloc (n * 4)
    in let nb = gpu-buf-alloc (n * 4)
    in let ok = x2 /= 0 & nb /= 0 & gpu-buf-read (mom.ah) 0 (8 * hw * 4) gm & noise-torch-cpu-into ge (i2-torch-seed (r.ti-seed)) n == 0
    in let p = if ok then img2img-posterior gm ge init hw (i2-latent-scale (hc.tc-sd15)) 0 else 0
    in let f = vd-free mom
    in let steps = if q.i2-hr-steps > 0 then q.i2-hr-steps else r.ti-steps
    in let hsig = img2img-sigmas-for (i2-hr-base q) (hc.tc-sd15) steps (q.i2-hr-denoise) True
    in if ok == False | gpu-buf-write x2 0 (n * 4) init == False | va-noise nb (r.ti-seed) (q.i2-var) 4 (mom.ahh) (mom.aww) == False then i2-fail "the hires latent could not be staged"
    else let s1 = sm-lincomb x2 nb nb x2 1.0 (list-at hsig 0) 0.0 n
    in let fb = gpu-buf-free nb
    in let bad2 = i2-sample-with (i2-hr-base q) cur x2 hsig (img2img-full-for (i2-hr-base q) (hc.tc-sd15) steps (q.i2-hr-denoise) True) n (\xh s -> i2-den (cur 0) xh s)
    in if bad2 > 0 then i2-fail ("hires sampling failed: " & show bad2 & " refused steps")
    else I2Start { is-x = x2, is-rgb = 0, is-mfo = 0, is-why = "" }
  i2-hires-size : Integer, Real -> Integer
  i2-hires-size (v) (scale) = real-to-int (real-from-int v * scale)

 One request against a checkpoint that is already loaded; everything else it
 allocates on the device it frees.

  img2img-with : ClipBpe, I2Model, I2i -> Text
  img2img-with (bpe) (m) (q) = if m.im-why /= "" then m.im-why else if q.i2-out-mk2 == 1 then i2-mk2 bpe m q else i2-go bpe m q

  i2-go : ClipBpe, I2Model, I2i -> Text
  i2-go (bpe) (m) (q) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let hires = q.i2-hr-scale > 0.0
    in let fh = if hires then i2-hires-size (r.ti-height) (q.i2-hr-scale) else r.ti-height
    in let fw = if hires then i2-hires-size (r.ti-width) (q.i2-hr-scale) else r.ti-width
    in let c = if m.im-sd15 then clip-condition-l (m.im-wl) bpe (r.ti-prompt) else clip-condition (m.im-wl) (m.im-wg) bpe (r.ti-prompt) False
    in let un = if m.im-sd15 then clip-condition-l (m.im-wl) bpe (r.ti-negative) else clip-condition (m.im-wl) (m.im-wg) bpe (r.ti-negative) True
    in if c.cn-status /= 0 | un.cn-status /= 0 then "text encoders failed " & show (c.cn-status) & " " & show (un.cn-status)
    else if c.cn-chunks /= 1 | un.cn-chunks /= 1 then "refused: prompt " & show (c.cn-chunks) & " chunks, negative " & show (un.cn-chunks) & "; the UNet context is one 77-token chunk"
    else let hp = if hires & q.i2-hr-prompt /= "" then q.i2-hr-prompt else r.ti-prompt
    in let hn = if hires & q.i2-hr-negative /= "" then q.i2-hr-negative else r.ti-negative
    in let same = hp == r.ti-prompt & hn == r.ti-negative
    in let c2 = if same then c else (if m.im-sd15 then clip-condition-l (m.im-wl) bpe hp else clip-condition (m.im-wl) (m.im-wg) bpe hp False)
    in let un2 = if same then un else (if m.im-sd15 then clip-condition-l (m.im-wl) bpe hn else clip-condition (m.im-wl) (m.im-wg) bpe hn True)
    in if c2.cn-status /= 0 | un2.cn-status /= 0 | c2.cn-chunks /= 1 | un2.cn-chunks /= 1 then "refused: the hires prompt and negative must each encode to one 77-token chunk"
    else if m.im-sd15 then i2-sample-all q m (c.cn-cond-l) (un.cn-cond-l) 0 0 0 0 (c2.cn-cond-l) (un2.cn-cond-l) fh fw (if same then [c.cn-cond-l, un.cn-cond-l] else [c.cn-cond-l, un.cn-cond-l, c2.cn-cond-l, un2.cn-cond-l])
    else let cc = clip-crossattn c
    in let cu = clip-crossattn un
    in let yc = ti-adm (c.cn-pooled) (r.ti-height) (r.ti-width)
    in let yu = ti-adm (un.cn-pooled) (r.ti-height) (r.ti-width)
    in let cc2 = if same then cc else clip-crossattn c2
    in let cu2 = if same then cu else clip-crossattn un2
    in let yc2 = if hires then ti-adm (c2.cn-pooled) fh fw else yc
    in let yu2 = if hires then ti-adm (un2.cn-pooled) fh fw else yu
    in let f1 = clip-cond-free c + clip-cond-free un + (if same then 0 else clip-cond-free c2 + clip-cond-free un2)
    in if cc == 0 | cu == 0 | yc == 0 | yu == 0 | yc2 == 0 | yu2 == 0 | cc2 == 0 | cu2 == 0 then "conditioning failed"
    else i2-sample-all q m cc cu yc yu yc2 yu2 cc2 cu2 fh fw (if hires then (if same then [cc, cu, yc, yu, yc2, yu2] else [cc, cu, yc, yu, yc2, yu2, cc2, cu2]) else [cc, cu, yc, yu])

 SD1.5's context is CLIP-L's cond as it stands and it takes no ADM vector,
 therefore its y handles are 0.

  i2-sample-all : I2i, I2Model, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> Text
  i2-sample-all (q) (m) (cc) (cu) (yc) (yu) (yc2) (yu2) (cc2) (cu2) (fh) (fw) (frees) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let u = m.im-unet
    in let tc = TiCfg { tc-unet = u, tc-tab = m.im-tab, tc-yc = yc, tc-cc = cc, tc-yu = yu, tc-cu = cu, tc-h = r.ti-height / 8, tc-w = r.ti-width / 8, tc-cfg = r.ti-cfg, tc-sd15 = m.im-sd15, tc-extras = r.ti-extras }
    in let hc = TiCfg { tc-unet = u, tc-tab = m.im-tab, tc-yc = yc2, tc-cc = cc2, tc-yu = yu2, tc-cu = cu2, tc-h = fh / 8, tc-w = fw / 8, tc-cfg = q.i2-hr-cfg, tc-sd15 = m.im-sd15, tc-extras = r.ti-extras }
    in if q.i2-out-px > 0 then (let res = i2-outpaint q tc m in let f0 = ti-free-all frees 0 0 in res)
    else let st = if q.i2-hr-scale > 0.0 then (if q.i2-hr-upscaler == "" then i2-hires q tc hc else i2-hires-upscaled q tc hc m) else if q.i2-image /= "" then i2-from-picture q tc m (\k -> tc) else i2-plain q tc
    in let f2 = ti-free-all frees 0 0
    in if st.is-x == 0 then st.is-why
    else i2-finish q st fh fw m

  img2img : ClipBpe, I2i -> Text
  img2img (bpe) (q) =
    let m = i2-skip (img2img-model ((q.i2-base).ti-ckpt)) ((q.i2-base).ti-clip-skip)
    in let res = img2img-with bpe m q
    in let f = img2img-model-free m
    in res

  i2-finish : I2i, I2Start, Integer, Integer, I2Model -> Text
  i2-finish (q) (st) (fh) (fw) (m) = i2-finish-with q st fh fw m ((q.i2-base).ti-params)

  i2-finish-with : I2i, I2Start, Integer, Integer, I2Model, Text -> Text
  i2-finish-with (q) (st) (fh) (fw) (m) (params) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let x = st.is-x
    in let z = sm-lincomb x x x x (1.0 / i2-latent-scale (m.im-sd15)) 0.0 0.0 (4 * (fh / 8) * (fw / 8))
    in let img = vae-decode (m.im-vd) (Act { ah = x, ac = 4, ahh = fh / 8, aww = fw / 8 })
    in if img.ah == 0 then "decode failed"
    else let rgb = st.is-rgb
    in let mfo = st.is-mfo
    in let only = rgb /= 0 & q.i2-area == 1
    in let sw = if only & q.i2-src-w > 0 then q.i2-src-w else fw
    in let sh = if only & q.i2-src-h > 0 then q.i2-src-h else fh
    in let bytes = if rgb == 0 then png-save img (r.ti-out) params else if only then i2-masked-save q img rgb mfo fw fh sw sh params else png-save-with img (r.ti-out) params (\i b -> i2-over (peek-byte rgb i) (255 - peek-byte mfo (i / 3)) b)
    in let f4 = vd-free img & gpu-buf-free x
    in if bytes < 0 then "save refused" else "png " & show sw & "x" & show sh & ": " & show bytes & " bytes"

 Forge's uncrop and apply_overlay: the result resized into the box of a
 picture-sized canvas, the picture's own overlay composited over it.

  i2-masked-save : I2i, Act, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Integer
  i2-masked-save (q) (img) (src) (m0) (fw) (fh) (sw) (sh) (params) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let gen = image-bytes img
    in if gen == 0 then 0 - 1
    else let bm = if q.i2-soft == 1 then i2-mask-blurred q sw sh sw sh else m0
    in png-save-rgb (img2img-composite src m0 (inpaint-uncrop gen fw fh (i2-box q bm sw sh fw fh) sw sh) 0 (sw * sh * 3)) sw sh (r.ti-out) params

Page 1

Section: Refiner

 Forge's apply_refiner (Diffusion.md, "Guidance and seeds"): the count of
 model calls so far over the steps, doubled for the
 samplers Forge marks second_order (DPM++ SDE, DPM++ 2S a, Heun, DPM2, DPM2 a,
 Restart), and the first call at or past the switch frees the base, loads
 the refiner and conditions on its text encoders for every later call; the
 picture decodes through the refiner's VAE. The base and the refiner are
 each loaded here, therefore the resident model is freed before.

  i2-second-order : Integer -> Boolean
  i2-second-order (s) = s == 1 | s == 5 | s == 9 | s == 10 | s == 11 | s == 14

  I2Cond = record {
    ic-tc : TiCfg,
    ic-frees : List Integer,
    ic-why : Text
  }

  i2-conds : ClipBpe, I2Model, Txt2Img -> I2Cond
  i2-conds (bpe) (m) (r) = i2-conds-at bpe m (r.ti-prompt) (r.ti-negative) (r.ti-height) (r.ti-width) (r.ti-cfg) (r.ti-extras)

  i2-conds-at : ClipBpe, I2Model, Text, Text, Integer, Integer, Real, TiExtras -> I2Cond
  i2-conds-at (bpe) (m) (p) (ng) (h) (w) (cfg) (ex) =
    let c = if m.im-sd15 then clip-condition-l (m.im-wl) bpe p else clip-condition (m.im-wl) (m.im-wg) bpe p False
    in let un = if m.im-sd15 then clip-condition-l (m.im-wl) bpe ng else clip-condition (m.im-wl) (m.im-wg) bpe ng True
    in let ok = c.cn-status == 0 & un.cn-status == 0 & c.cn-chunks == 1 & un.cn-chunks == 1
    in let cc = if ok == False then 0 else if m.im-sd15 then c.cn-cond-l else clip-crossattn c
    in let cu = if ok == False then 0 else if m.im-sd15 then un.cn-cond-l else clip-crossattn un
    in let yc = if ok & m.im-sd15 == False then ti-adm (c.cn-pooled) h w else 0
    in let yu = if ok & m.im-sd15 == False then ti-adm (un.cn-pooled) h w else 0
    in let f = if m.im-sd15 & ok then 0 else clip-cond-free c + clip-cond-free un
    in let tc = TiCfg { tc-unet = m.im-unet, tc-tab = m.im-tab, tc-yc = yc, tc-cc = cc, tc-yu = yu, tc-cu = cu, tc-h = h / 8, tc-w = w / 8, tc-cfg = cfg, tc-sd15 = m.im-sd15, tc-extras = ex }
    in I2Cond { ic-tc = tc, ic-frees = (if m.im-sd15 then [cc, cu] else [cc, cu, yc, yu]), ic-why = if ok & cc /= 0 & cu /= 0 & (m.im-sd15 | (yc /= 0 & yu /= 0)) then "" else "conditioning failed" }

 The model in use, its configuration and the condition buffers to free are
 one-element lists the denoiser replaces at the switch; calls holds the count
 of model calls and whether the switch is done.

  RefPass = record {
    rp-prompt : Text,
    rp-negative : Text,
    rp-h : Integer,
    rp-w : Integer,
    rp-cfg : Real
  }

  RefState = record {
    rs-calls : List Integer,
    rs-models : List I2Model,
    rs-cfgs : List TiCfg,
    rs-frees : List (List Integer),
    rs-pass : RefPass
  }

 At the switch Forge re-activates the prompt's networks on the refiner and
 then conditions the pass's prompt on it (sd_samplers_common.py:201-204).

  i2-ref-swap : ClipBpe, I2i, RefState, (I2Model -> Integer) -> TiCfg
  i2-ref-swap (bpe) (q) (st) (lora) =
    let f1 = ti-free-all (list-at (st.rs-frees) 0) 0 0 + img2img-model-free (list-at (st.rs-models) 0)
    in let f2 = un-pool-drain 0 + gpu-buf-pool-drain 0
    in let m1 = i2-skip (img2img-model (q.i2-refiner)) ((q.i2-base).ti-clip-skip)
    in let lw = if m1.im-why == "" & m1.im-sd15 == False then lora m1 else 0
    in let p = st.rs-pass
    in let cd = if m1.im-why == "" & m1.im-sd15 == False & lw >= 0 then i2-conds-at bpe m1 (p.rp-prompt) (p.rp-negative) (p.rp-h) (p.rp-w) (p.rp-cfg) ti-no-extras else I2Cond { ic-tc = i2-no-cfg m1, ic-frees = [], ic-why = "refused: the refiner is not an SDXL checkpoint, or a LoRA could not be merged" }
    in let a = list-set-at (st.rs-models) 0 m1
    in let b = list-set-at (st.rs-cfgs) 0 (cd.ic-tc)
    in let c = list-set-at (st.rs-frees) 0 (cd.ic-frees)
    in let d = list-set-at (st.rs-calls) 1 1
    in cd.ic-tc

  i2-ref-cfg : ClipBpe, I2i, RefState, Integer, (I2Model -> Integer) -> TiCfg
  i2-ref-cfg (bpe) (q) (st) (total) (lora) =
    let k = list-at (st.rs-calls) 0
    in let c = list-set-at (st.rs-calls) 0 (k + 1)
    in if list-at (st.rs-calls) 1 == 1 | real-from-int k / real-from-int total < q.i2-switch then list-at (st.rs-cfgs) 0
    else i2-ref-swap bpe q st lora

 The refiner for text to image, img2img and inpaint, and hires fix, where
 Forge's default hires_fix_refiner_pass, "second pass", applies it to the
 hires pass alone (sd_samplers_common.py:174-181). The switch counts the
 pass's model calls against its total_steps (launch_sampling): the steps for
 text to image, t_enc + 1 for img2img and the hires pass, doubled for a
 second-order sampler.

  img2img-refined : ClipBpe, I2i, (I2Model -> Integer), Text -> Text
  img2img-refined (bpe) (q) (lora) (keys) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let hires = q.i2-hr-scale > 0.0
    in let fh = if hires then i2-hires-size (r.ti-height) (q.i2-hr-scale) else r.ti-height
    in let fw = if hires then i2-hires-size (r.ti-width) (q.i2-hr-scale) else r.ti-width
    in let m0 = i2-skip (img2img-model (r.ti-ckpt)) (r.ti-clip-skip)
    in let lw = if m0.im-why == "" then lora m0 else 0
    in let why = if m0.im-why /= "" then m0.im-why else if m0.im-sd15 then "refused: the refiner is for SDXL here" else if lw < 0 then "refused: a LoRA could not be merged" else ""
    in let cd = if why == "" then i2-conds bpe m0 r else I2Cond { ic-tc = i2-no-cfg m0, ic-frees = [], ic-why = why }
    in let pass = if hires then RefPass { rp-prompt = (if q.i2-hr-prompt /= "" then q.i2-hr-prompt else r.ti-prompt), rp-negative = (if q.i2-hr-negative /= "" then q.i2-hr-negative else r.ti-negative), rp-h = fh, rp-w = fw, rp-cfg = q.i2-hr-cfg } else RefPass { rp-prompt = r.ti-prompt, rp-negative = r.ti-negative, rp-h = fh, rp-w = fw, rp-cfg = r.ti-cfg }
    in let hd = if hires & cd.ic-why == "" then i2-conds-at bpe m0 (pass.rp-prompt) (pass.rp-negative) fh fw (pass.rp-cfg) (r.ti-extras) else cd
    in let st = RefState { rs-calls = [0, if q.i2-refiner == r.ti-ckpt then 1 else 0], rs-models = [m0], rs-cfgs = [hd.ic-tc], rs-frees = [(if hires then cd.ic-frees & hd.ic-frees else cd.ic-frees)], rs-pass = pass }
    in let cur = \k -> i2-ref-cfg bpe q st (i2-ref-total q) lora
    in let start = if hd.ic-why /= "" then i2-fail (hd.ic-why) else if hires then i2-ref-hires q (cd.ic-tc) (hd.ic-tc) m0 cur else if q.i2-image /= "" then i2-from-picture q (cd.ic-tc) m0 cur else i2-ref-plain q (cd.ic-tc) cur
    in let m = list-at (st.rs-models) 0
    in let switched = list-at (st.rs-calls) 1 == 1 & q.i2-refiner /= r.ti-ckpt
    in let res = if start.is-x == 0 then start.is-why else i2-finish-with q start fh fw m (if switched then r.ti-params & keys else r.ti-params)
    in let f = ti-free-all (list-at (st.rs-frees) 0) 0 0 + img2img-model-free m
    in res

  i2-ref-total : I2i -> Integer
  i2-ref-total (q) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let h = i2-hr-base q
    in if q.i2-hr-scale > 0.0 then (if q.i2-hr-steps > 0 then q.i2-hr-steps else r.ti-steps) * (if i2-second-order (h.ti-sampler) then 2 else 1)
    else if q.i2-image /= "" then (list-at (img2img-plan (r.ti-steps) (q.i2-denoise) False) 1 + 1) * (if i2-second-order (r.ti-sampler) then 2 else 1)
    else r.ti-steps * (if i2-second-order (r.ti-sampler) then 2 else 1)

  i2-ref-plain : I2i, TiCfg, (Integer -> TiCfg) -> I2Start
  i2-ref-plain (q) (tc) (cur) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let n = 4 * tc.tc-h * tc.tc-w
    in let x = gpu-buf-alloc (n * 4)
    in let ok = x /= 0 & va-noise x (r.ti-seed) (q.i2-var) 4 (tc.tc-h) (tc.tc-w)
    in let bad = if ok == False then 1 else ti-txt2img-run-with r tc x n (\xh s -> i2-den (cur 0) xh s) (\xh s ub -> ti-den3 (cur 0) xh s ub)
    in if bad > 0 then i2-fail ("sampling failed: " & show bad & " refused steps") else I2Start { is-x = x, is-rgb = 0, is-mfo = 0, is-why = "" }

  i2-ref-hires : I2i, TiCfg, TiCfg, I2Model, (Integer -> TiCfg) -> I2Start
  i2-ref-hires (q) (tc) (hc) (m0) (cur) =
    if q.i2-hr-upscaler == "" then (let f = i2-first-latent q tc (hc.tc-h) (hc.tc-w) in if f.is-rgb == 0 then f else i2-hires-latent q hc (f.is-rgb) cur)
    else (let f = i2-first-bytes q tc m0 in if f.is-rgb == 0 then f else i2-hires-picture q tc hc m0 (f.is-rgb) cur)

Section: Outpainting

 Forge's poor man's outpainting (scripts/poor_mans_outpainting.py): the
 picture on a black canvas of multiples of 64, grown by pixels on each chosen
 side, the growth split between opposite sides as left (W - w) // (left +
 right) and the rest; an image mask white but for a black rectangle inset 2
 blur from each grown side and a latent mask inset blur // 2, each
 rectangle's corners inclusive (ImageDraw); split_grid into request-sized
 tiles overlapping by pixels (x = int (col dx), dx = (W - tile) / (cols - 1)
 in floating point, clamped to the last whole tile), every tile not wholly
 inside the picture inpainted with mask blur 2 blur and the latent mask for
 fill and for the latent, at seed plus its index; combine_grid joins them.
 Forge's CPU generator gives a tile's posterior the previous tile's seed and
 the first tile the last tile's of the run before (a request's second run).

  i2-ceil64 : Integer -> Integer
  i2-ceil64 (v) = (v + 63) / 64 * 64

  OutPlan = record {
    op-l : Integer,
    op-r : Integer,
    op-u : Integer,
    op-d : Integer,
    op-w : Integer,
    op-h : Integer
  }

  i2-out-plan : I2i, Integer, Integer -> OutPlan
  i2-out-plan (q) (sw) (sh) =
    let px = q.i2-out-px
    in let l0 = if bit-and (q.i2-out-dirs) 1 /= 0 then px else 0
    in let r0 = if bit-and (q.i2-out-dirs) 2 /= 0 then px else 0
    in let u0 = if bit-and (q.i2-out-dirs) 4 /= 0 then px else 0
    in let d0 = if bit-and (q.i2-out-dirs) 8 /= 0 then px else 0
    in let tw = i2-ceil64 (sw + l0 + r0)
    in let th = i2-ceil64 (sh + u0 + d0)
    in let l = if l0 > 0 then l0 * (tw - sw) / (l0 + r0) else 0
    in let u = if u0 > 0 then u0 * (th - sh) / (u0 + d0) else 0
    in OutPlan { op-l = l, op-r = (if r0 > 0 then tw - sw - l else 0), op-u = u, op-d = (if d0 > 0 then th - sh - u else 0), op-w = tw, op-h = th }

  i2-canvas : Integer, Integer, Integer, OutPlan, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-canvas (src) (sw) (sh) (pl) (dst) (i) =
    if i >= pl.op-w * pl.op-h * 3 then dst
    else let y = i / (pl.op-w * 3)
    in let x = (i - y * pl.op-w * 3) / 3
    in let c = i - y * pl.op-w * 3 - x * 3
    in let inside = x >= pl.op-l & x < pl.op-l + sw & y >= pl.op-u & y < pl.op-u + sh
    in let s = poke-byte dst i (if inside then peek-byte src (((y - pl.op-u) * sw + x - pl.op-l) * 3 + c) else 0)
    in i2-canvas src sw sh pl dst (i + 1)

  i2-rect : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-rect (dst) (w) (h) (x0) (y0) (x1) (y1) (i) =
    if i >= w * h then dst
    else let y = i / w
    in let x = i - y * w
    in let s = poke-byte dst i (if x >= x0 & x <= x1 & y >= y0 & y <= y1 then 0 else 255)
    in i2-rect dst w h x0 y0 x1 y1 (i + 1)

  i2-out-mask : OutPlan, Integer -> Integer
  i2-out-mask (pl) (b) = i2-rect (alloc-bytes (pl.op-w * pl.op-h)) (pl.op-w) (pl.op-h) (pl.op-l + (if pl.op-l > 0 then b else 0)) (pl.op-u + (if pl.op-u > 0 then b else 0)) (pl.op-w - pl.op-r - (if pl.op-r > 0 then b else 0)) (pl.op-h - pl.op-d - (if pl.op-d > 0 then b else 0)) 0

  i2-crop : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-crop (src) (sw) (ch) (x) (y) (w) (h) (dst) (i) =
    if i >= w * h * ch then dst
    else let yy = i / (w * ch)
    in let s = poke-byte dst i (peek-byte src (((y + yy) * sw + x) * ch + i - yy * w * ch))
    in i2-crop src sw ch x y w h dst (i + 1)

  i2-grid-starts : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  i2-grid-starts (n) (tile) (count) (k) (acc) =
    if k >= count then acc
    else let x = if count > 1 then real-to-int (real-from-int k * (real-from-int (n - tile) / real-from-int (count - 1))) else 0
    in i2-grid-starts n tile count (k + 1) (list-push acc (if x + tile >= n then n - tile else x))

  i2-interior : OutPlan, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  i2-interior (pl) (x) (y) (w) (h) = x >= pl.op-l & x + w <= pl.op-w - pl.op-r & y >= pl.op-u & y + h <= pl.op-h - pl.op-d

  i2-work-count : OutPlan, List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-work-count (pl) (xs) (ys) (w) (h) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length xs * list-length ys then acc
    else let x = list-at xs (i - i / list-length xs * list-length xs)
    in let y = list-at ys (i / list-length xs)
    in i2-work-count pl xs ys w h (i + 1) (if i2-interior pl x y w h then acc else acc + 1)

  i2-reseed : I2i, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> I2i
  i2-reseed (q) (seed) (post) (w) (h) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let b = Txt2Img { ti-ckpt = r.ti-ckpt, ti-prompt = r.ti-prompt, ti-negative = r.ti-negative, ti-sampler = r.ti-sampler, ti-scheduler = r.ti-scheduler, ti-steps = r.ti-steps, ti-cfg = r.ti-cfg, ti-seed = seed, ti-width = w, ti-height = h, ti-out = r.ti-out, ti-params = r.ti-params, ti-clip-skip = r.ti-clip-skip, ti-extras = r.ti-extras }
    in I2i { i2-base = b, i2-image = q.i2-image, i2-mask = "", i2-denoise = q.i2-denoise, i2-blur = q.i2-blur, i2-hr-scale = 0.0, i2-hr-denoise = q.i2-hr-denoise, i2-hr-steps = q.i2-hr-steps, i2-hr-cfg = q.i2-hr-cfg, i2-hr-upscaler = "", i2-var = q.i2-var, i2-src-w = 0, i2-src-h = 0, i2-resize = 0, i2-fill = q.i2-fill, i2-area = 0, i2-padding = q.i2-padding, i2-refiner = "", i2-switch = q.i2-switch, i2-hr-sampler = q.i2-hr-sampler, i2-hr-scheduler = q.i2-hr-scheduler, i2-hr-prompt = "", i2-hr-negative = "", i2-hr-ckpt = "", i2-hr-vae = "", i2-soft = 0, i2-sc = q.i2-sc, i2-out-px = 0, i2-out-blur = 0, i2-out-dirs = 0, i2-post = post, i2-out-mk2 = 0, i2-out-q = q.i2-out-q, i2-out-cv = q.i2-out-cv }

  i2-tile-bytes : I2Start, I2Model, Integer, Integer -> I2Start
  i2-tile-bytes (st) (m) (w) (h) =
    let x = st.is-x
    in let z = sm-lincomb x x x x (1.0 / i2-latent-scale (m.im-sd15)) 0.0 0.0 (4 * (w / 8) * (h / 8))
    in let img = vae-decode (m.im-vd) (Act { ah = x, ac = 4, ahh = h / 8, aww = w / 8 })
    in let fx = gpu-buf-free x
    in if img.ah == 0 then i2-fail "decode failed"
    else let gen = image-bytes img
    in let fi = vd-free img
    in if gen == 0 then i2-fail "decode failed"
    else I2Start { is-x = 0, is-rgb = img2img-composite (st.is-rgb) (st.is-mfo) gen 0 (w * h * 3), is-mfo = 0, is-why = "" }

  i2-out-tile : I2i, TiCfg, I2Model, Integer, Integer, Integer, OutPlan, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> I2Start
  i2-out-tile (q) (tc) (m) (cv) (mk) (lk) (pl) (x) (y) (seed) (post) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let w = r.ti-width
    in let h = r.ti-height
    in let qq = i2-reseed q seed post w h
    in let rgb = i2-crop cv (pl.op-w) 3 x y w h (alloc-bytes (w * h * 3)) 0
    in let msk = i2-crop mk (pl.op-w) 1 x y w h (alloc-bytes (w * h)) 0
    in let lmk = i2-crop lk (pl.op-w) 1 x y w h (alloc-bytes (w * h)) 0
    in let blurred = img2img-blur msk w h (2 * q.i2-out-blur)
    in let pic = img2img-picture (if q.i2-fill == 0 then inpaint-fill rgb lmk w h else rgb) h w
    in let mom = if pic.ah == 0 then pic else vae-encode (m.im-ve) pic
    in let f = vd-free pic
    in if mom.ah == 0 then i2-fail "encode failed"
    else let st = i2-with-moments qq tc rgb mom lmk (img2img-overlay-mask blurred (w * h)) (\k -> tc)
    in if st.is-x == 0 then st else i2-tile-bytes st m w h

  i2-out-cols : I2i, TiCfg, I2Model, Integer, Integer, Integer, OutPlan, List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-out-cols (q) (tc) (m) (cv) (mk) (lk) (pl) (xs) (y) (i) (k) (n) (row) =
    if i >= list-length xs then k
    else let r = q.i2-base
    in let w = r.ti-width
    in let h = r.ti-height
    in let x = list-at xs i
    in let inner = i2-interior pl x y w h
    in let st = if inner then I2Start { is-x = 0, is-rgb = i2-crop cv (pl.op-w) 3 x y w h (alloc-bytes (w * h * 3)) 0, is-mfo = 0, is-why = "" } else i2-out-tile q tc m cv mk lk pl x y (r.ti-seed + k) (r.ti-seed + (if k == 0 then n - 1 else k - 1))
    in if st.is-rgb == 0 then 0 - 1
    else let p = esr-paste row (pl.op-w) (st.is-rgb) w h x 0 (if x == 0 then 0 else q.i2-out-px) 0 0
    in i2-out-cols q tc m cv mk lk pl xs y (i + 1) (if inner then k else k + 1) n row

  i2-out-rows : I2i, TiCfg, I2Model, Integer, Integer, Integer, OutPlan, List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-out-rows (q) (tc) (m) (cv) (mk) (lk) (pl) (xs) (ys) (j) (k) (n) (out) =
    if j >= list-length ys then k
    else let h = (q.i2-base).ti-height
    in let y = list-at ys j
    in let row = alloc-bytes (pl.op-w * h * 3)
    in let k2 = i2-out-cols q tc m cv mk lk pl xs y 0 k n row
    in if k2 < 0 then k2
    else let p = esr-paste out (pl.op-w) row (pl.op-w) h 0 y 0 (if y == 0 then 0 else q.i2-out-px) 0
    in i2-out-rows q tc m cv mk lk pl xs ys (j + 1) k2 n out

  i2-outpaint : I2i, TiCfg, I2Model -> Text
  i2-outpaint (q) (tc) (m) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let w = r.ti-width
    in let h = r.ti-height
    in let sw = if q.i2-src-w > 0 then q.i2-src-w else w
    in let sh = if q.i2-src-h > 0 then q.i2-src-h else h
    in let pl = i2-out-plan q sw sh
    in if pl.op-w < w | pl.op-h < h then "refused: the outpainted canvas " & show (pl.op-w) & "x" & show (pl.op-h) & " is smaller than the tile " & show w & "x" & show h
    else let px = i2-read-file (q.i2-image) (sw * sh * 4)
    in if px == 0 then "refused: the picture could not be read"
    else let cv = i2-canvas (i2-rgb-bytes px (alloc-bytes (sw * sh * 3)) 0 (sw * sh * 3)) sw sh pl (alloc-bytes (pl.op-w * pl.op-h * 3)) 0
    in let mk = i2-out-mask pl (2 * q.i2-out-blur)
    in let lk = i2-out-mask pl (q.i2-out-blur / 2)
    in let ov = q.i2-out-px
    in let xs = i2-grid-starts (pl.op-w) w (esr-count (pl.op-w) w ov) 0 []
    in let ys = i2-grid-starts (pl.op-h) h (esr-count (pl.op-h) h ov) 0 []
    in let out = alloc-bytes (pl.op-w * pl.op-h * 3)
    in let k = i2-out-rows q tc m cv mk lk pl xs ys 0 0 (i2-work-count pl xs ys w h 0 0) out
    in if k < 0 then "outpainting failed at a tile"
    else let bytes = png-save-rgb out (pl.op-w) (pl.op-h) (r.ti-out) (r.ti-params)
    in if bytes < 0 then "save refused" else "png " & show (pl.op-w) & "x" & show (pl.op-h) & ": " & show bytes & " bytes"

Section: Outpainting mk2

 Forge's outpainting mk2 (scripts/outpainting_mk_2.py): the chosen sides in
 the order left, right, up, down, each on the picture the last one left.
 Each side: the picture on a black canvas of the side's growth rounded up to
 multiples of 64, at the grown edge; an RGB mask white but for a black
 rectangle from pixels plus blur in from each side being grown to the
 picture's far edge (corners inclusive), where blur is the mask blur on the
 axis of any horizontal (or vertical) side chosen and 0 on the other; the
 canvas filled by get_matched_noise and truncated to bytes; the region of
 the grown edge min (request, grown) wide on that axis and the canvas's size
 on the other, inpainted with that mask cropped, blurred 4 blur across and 4
 blur down, masked content original, the same seed, and a latent mask of
 the same shape inset 2 blur; the result pasted back and the canvas cropped
 to the grown size. The conditioning is the pass's own size's.

  i2-blur-xy : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-blur-xy (m) (w) (h) (bx) (by) =
    let a = if bx > 0 then i2-blur-pass m (alloc-bytes (w * h)) w h True (i2-gauss bx) 0 else m
    in if by > 0 then i2-blur-pass a (alloc-bytes (w * h)) w h False (i2-gauss by) 0 else a

  i2-to-reals : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-to-reals (bytes) (dst) (i) (n) = if i >= n then dst else let s = md-set dst i (real-from-int (peek-byte bytes i) / 255.0) in i2-to-reals bytes dst (i + 1) n

  i2-mask-reals : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-mask-reals (m) (dst) (i) (n) = if i >= n then dst else let v = real-from-int (peek-byte m (i / 3)) / 255.0 in let s = md-set dst i v in i2-mask-reals m dst (i + 1) n

  i2-to-bytes : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-to-bytes (vals) (dst) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then dst
    else let c = md-get vals i * 255.0
    in let s = poke-byte dst i (real-to-int (if c < 0.0 then 0.0 else if c > 255.0 then 255.0 else c))
    in i2-to-bytes vals dst (i + 1) n

  i2-paste : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-paste (dst) (dw) (src) (sw) (sh) (x) (y) (i) =
    if i >= sw * sh * 3 then dst
    else let yy = i / (sw * 3)
    in let s = poke-byte dst (((y + yy) * dw + x) * 3 + i - yy * sw * 3) (peek-byte src i)
    in i2-paste dst dw src sw sh x y (i + 1)

  Mk2Side = record {
    ms-left : Boolean,
    ms-right : Boolean,
    ms-top : Boolean,
    ms-bottom : Boolean
  }

  i2-mk2-bx : I2i -> Integer
  i2-mk2-bx (q) = if bit-and (q.i2-out-dirs) 3 /= 0 then q.i2-out-blur else 0

  i2-mk2-by : I2i -> Integer
  i2-mk2-by (q) = if bit-and (q.i2-out-dirs) 12 /= 0 then q.i2-out-blur else 0

 One side's expand; the grown picture as bytes, or 0 with the reason in why.

  i2-mk2-side : ClipBpe, I2Model, I2i, Integer, Integer, Integer, Mk2Side, List Text -> Integer
  i2-mk2-side (bpe) (m) (q) (img) (cw) (ch) (sd) (why) =
    let px = q.i2-out-px
    in let horiz = sd.ms-left | sd.ms-right
    in let ph = if horiz then px else 0
    in let pv = if horiz then 0 else px
    in let rw = cw + ph
    in let rh = ch + pv
    in let pw = i2-ceil64 rw
    in let phh = i2-ceil64 rh
    in let bx = i2-mk2-bx q
    in let by = i2-mk2-by q
    in let r = q.i2-base
    in let tw = if horiz then (if r.ti-width < rw then r.ti-width else rw) else pw
    in let th = if horiz then phh else (if r.ti-height < rh then r.ti-height else rh)
    in if tw * th > 1048576 | int-mod tw 64 /= 0 | int-mod th 64 /= 0 then (let w = list-set-at why 0 ("refused: an outpainting pass of " & show tw & "x" & show th & " (multiples of 64, at most 1024x1024 pixels)") in 0)
    else let cv = i2-paste (i2-zero-bytes (alloc-bytes (pw * phh * 3)) 0 (pw * phh * 3)) pw img cw ch (if sd.ms-left then ph else 0) (if sd.ms-top then pv else 0) 0
    in let mk = i2-rect (alloc-bytes (pw * phh)) pw phh (if sd.ms-left then px + bx else 0) (if sd.ms-top then px + by else 0) (if sd.ms-right then pw - px - bx else rw) (if sd.ms-bottom then phh - px - by else rh) 0
    in let noised = i2-to-bytes (matched-noise (i2-to-reals cv (md-new (pw * phh * 3)) 0 (pw * phh * 3)) (i2-mask-reals mk (md-new (pw * phh * 3)) 0 (pw * phh * 3)) cv phh pw (q.i2-out-q) (q.i2-out-cv)) (alloc-bytes (pw * phh * 3)) 0 (pw * phh * 3)
    in let cx = if sd.ms-left then 0 else pw - tw
    in let cy = if sd.ms-top then 0 else phh - th
    in let part = i2-crop noised pw 3 cx cy tw th (alloc-bytes (tw * th * 3)) 0
    in let pmask = i2-crop mk pw 1 cx cy tw th (alloc-bytes (tw * th)) 0
    in let lmask = i2-rect (alloc-bytes (tw * th)) tw th (if sd.ms-left then px + 2 * bx else 0) (if sd.ms-top then px + 2 * by else 0) (if sd.ms-right then tw - px - 2 * bx else rw) (if sd.ms-bottom then th - px - 2 * by else rh) 0
    in let done = i2-mk2-pass bpe m q part pmask lmask tw th (4 * bx) (4 * by)
    in if done.is-rgb == 0 then (let w = list-set-at why 0 (done.is-why) in 0)
    else let back = i2-paste noised pw (done.is-rgb) tw th cx cy 0
    in i2-crop noised pw 3 0 0 rw rh (alloc-bytes (rw * rh * 3)) 0

  i2-zero-bytes : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  i2-zero-bytes (dst) (i) (n) = if i >= n then dst else let s = poke-byte dst i 0 in i2-zero-bytes dst (i + 1) n

  i2-mk2-pass : ClipBpe, I2Model, I2i, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> I2Start
  i2-mk2-pass (bpe) (m) (q) (img) (mask) (lmask) (tw) (th) (bx4) (by4) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let qq = i2-reseed q (r.ti-seed) (0 - 1) tw th
    in let cd = i2-conds-at bpe m (r.ti-prompt) (r.ti-negative) th tw (r.ti-cfg) (r.ti-extras)
    in if cd.ic-why /= "" then i2-fail (cd.ic-why)
    else let blurred = i2-blur-xy mask tw th bx4 by4
    in let pic = img2img-picture img th tw
    in let mom = if pic.ah == 0 then pic else vae-encode (m.im-ve) pic
    in let f = vd-free pic
    in let st = if mom.ah == 0 then i2-fail "encode failed" else i2-with-moments qq (cd.ic-tc) img mom lmask (img2img-overlay-mask blurred (tw * th)) (\k -> cd.ic-tc)
    in let f2 = ti-free-all (cd.ic-frees) 0 0
    in if st.is-x == 0 then st else i2-tile-bytes st m tw th

  i2-mk2-each : ClipBpe, I2Model, I2i, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Text -> Text
  i2-mk2-each (bpe) (m) (q) (img) (cw) (ch) (k) (why) =
    if k >= 4 then (let r = q.i2-base in let bytes = png-save-rgb img cw ch (r.ti-out) (r.ti-params) in if bytes < 0 then "save refused" else "png " & show cw & "x" & show ch & ": " & show bytes & " bytes")
    else if bit-and (q.i2-out-dirs) (bit-shl 1 k) == 0 then i2-mk2-each bpe m q img cw ch (k + 1) why
    else let sd = Mk2Side { ms-left = k == 0, ms-right = k == 1, ms-top = k == 2, ms-bottom = k == 3 }
    in let next = i2-mk2-side bpe m q img cw ch sd why
    in if next == 0 then list-at why 0
    else i2-mk2-each bpe m q next (if k < 2 then cw + q.i2-out-px else cw) (if k >= 2 then ch + q.i2-out-px else ch) (k + 1) why

  i2-mk2 : ClipBpe, I2Model, I2i -> Text
  i2-mk2 (bpe) (m) (q) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let sw = if q.i2-src-w > 0 then q.i2-src-w else r.ti-width
    in let sh = if q.i2-src-h > 0 then q.i2-src-h else r.ti-height
    in let px = i2-read-file (q.i2-image) (sw * sh * 4)
    in if px == 0 then "refused: the picture could not be read"
    else i2-mk2-each bpe m q (i2-rgb-bytes px (alloc-bytes (sw * sh * 3)) 0 (sw * sh * 3)) sw sh 0 ["mk2 failed"]

Section: Hires Checkpoint

 Forge's hr_checkpoint_name (processing.py:1279-1285, 1400-1428): the first
 pass samples on the base, and for an upscaler decodes through the base's VAE;
 then the hires checkpoint is loaded in its place, conditions the hires prompt
 on its own text encoders, samples the hires pass, encodes the upscaled
 picture and decodes the result; the prompt's networks are activated on each
 checkpoint as it loads. A refiner in the hires pass reloads only when it is
 neither the hires checkpoint nor the base, because checkpoint_change compares
 it with the configured checkpoint, the base (sd_samplers_common.py:171-199);
 a refiner that is the base writes its keys and changes nothing. The latent
 passes between the two unscaled,
 as Forge's samples do. Two checkpoints do not fit the card together,
 therefore the base is freed before the hires checkpoint loads, as in
 img2img-refined.

  img2img-hr-swapped : ClipBpe, I2i, (I2Model -> Integer), Text -> Text
  img2img-hr-swapped (bpe) (q) (lora) (keys) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let fh = i2-hires-size (r.ti-height) (q.i2-hr-scale)
    in let fw = i2-hires-size (r.ti-width) (q.i2-hr-scale)
    in let m0 = i2-skip (img2img-model (r.ti-ckpt)) (r.ti-clip-skip)
    in let why0 = if m0.im-why /= "" then m0.im-why else if lora m0 < 0 then "refused: a LoRA could not be merged" else ""
    in let c0 = if why0 == "" then i2-conds bpe m0 r else I2Cond { ic-tc = i2-no-cfg m0, ic-frees = [], ic-why = why0 }
    in let first = if c0.ic-why /= "" then i2-fail (c0.ic-why) else if q.i2-hr-upscaler == "" then i2-first-latent q (c0.ic-tc) (fh / 8) (fw / 8) else i2-first-bytes q (c0.ic-tc) m0
    in let f0 = ti-free-all (c0.ic-frees) 0 0 + img2img-model-free m0 + un-pool-drain 0 + gpu-buf-pool-drain 0
    in if first.is-rgb == 0 then first.is-why
    else i2-hr-second bpe q (first.is-rgb) fh fw lora keys

  i2-hr-second : ClipBpe, I2i, Integer, Integer, Integer, (I2Model -> Integer), Text -> Text
  i2-hr-second (bpe) (q) (first) (fh) (fw) (lora) (keys) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in let m1 = i2-skip (i2-with-vae (img2img-model (q.i2-hr-ckpt)) (q.i2-hr-vae)) ((q.i2-base).ti-clip-skip)
    in let hp = if q.i2-hr-prompt /= "" then q.i2-hr-prompt else r.ti-prompt
    in let hn = if q.i2-hr-negative /= "" then q.i2-hr-negative else r.ti-negative
    in let why1 = if m1.im-why /= "" then m1.im-why else if lora m1 < 0 then "refused: a LoRA could not be merged" else ""
    in let c1 = if why1 == "" then i2-conds-at bpe m1 hp hn fh fw (q.i2-hr-cfg) (r.ti-extras) else I2Cond { ic-tc = i2-no-cfg m1, ic-frees = [], ic-why = why1 }
    in let tc = TiCfg { tc-unet = m1.im-unet, tc-tab = m1.im-tab, tc-yc = 0, tc-cc = 0, tc-yu = 0, tc-cu = 0, tc-h = r.ti-height / 8, tc-w = r.ti-width / 8, tc-cfg = r.ti-cfg, tc-sd15 = m1.im-sd15, tc-extras = r.ti-extras }
    in let rs = RefState { rs-calls = [0, if q.i2-refiner == "" | q.i2-refiner == q.i2-hr-ckpt | q.i2-refiner == r.ti-ckpt then 1 else 0], rs-models = [m1], rs-cfgs = [c1.ic-tc], rs-frees = [c1.ic-frees], rs-pass = RefPass { rp-prompt = hp, rp-negative = hn, rp-h = fh, rp-w = fw, rp-cfg = q.i2-hr-cfg } }
    in let cur = \k -> i2-ref-cfg bpe q rs (i2-ref-total q) lora
    in let st = if c1.ic-why /= "" then i2-fail (c1.ic-why) else if q.i2-hr-upscaler == "" then i2-hires-latent q (c1.ic-tc) first cur else i2-hires-picture q tc (c1.ic-tc) m1 first cur
    in let mf = list-at (rs.rs-models) 0
    in let f1 = ti-free-all (list-at (rs.rs-frees) 0) 0 0
    in let reached = real-from-int (i2-ref-total q - 1) / real-from-int (i2-ref-total q) >= q.i2-switch
    in let switched = q.i2-refiner /= "" & q.i2-refiner /= q.i2-hr-ckpt & (if q.i2-refiner == r.ti-ckpt then reached else list-at (rs.rs-calls) 1 == 1)
    in let res = if st.is-x == 0 then st.is-why else i2-finish-with q st fh fw mf (if switched then r.ti-params & keys else r.ti-params)
    in let f2 = img2img-model-free mf
    in res

 Forge's hires VAE module (backend/loader.py:205-210): a file holding
 decoder.conv_in.weight replaces every key under the checkpoint's VAE prefix,
 therefore the hires model encodes and decodes through the file's VAE.

  i2-with-vae : I2Model, Text -> I2Model
  i2-with-vae (m) (path) =
    if path == "" | m.im-why /= "" then m
    else let file = ckpt-open path
    in let lb = layout-bind file sd-vae-file-layout
    in let ok = file.st-valid & parts-complete (lb.lb-parts) 0
    in let vpart = ti-vae-part (lb.lb-parts) 0
    in let f = if ok then vae-free (m.im-vd) 0 0 + vae-free (m.im-ve) 0 0 else 0
    in I2Model { im-ckpt = m.im-ckpt, im-why = (if ok then "" else "refused: " & path & " is not a readable SDXL or SD1.5 VAE"), im-sd15 = m.im-sd15, im-wl = m.im-wl, im-wg = m.im-wg, im-unet = m.im-unet, im-tab = m.im-tab, im-vd = (if ok then vae-load path vpart "" else m.im-vd), im-ve = (if ok then vae-encoder-load path vpart "" else m.im-ve) }

  i2-no-cfg : I2Model -> TiCfg
  i2-no-cfg (m) = TiCfg { tc-unet = m.im-unet, tc-tab = m.im-tab, tc-yc = 0, tc-cc = 0, tc-yu = 0, tc-cu = 0, tc-h = 0, tc-w = 0, tc-cfg = 1.0, tc-sd15 = m.im-sd15, tc-extras = ti-no-extras }

 The request as the hires pass runs it: the hires sampler and schedule where
 the request names them (Forge's hr_sampler_name, hr_scheduler), else the
 first pass's.

  i2-hr-base : I2i -> Txt2Img
  i2-hr-base (q) =
    let r = q.i2-base
    in Txt2Img { ti-ckpt = r.ti-ckpt, ti-prompt = r.ti-prompt, ti-negative = r.ti-negative, ti-sampler = (if q.i2-hr-sampler >= 0 then q.i2-hr-sampler else r.ti-sampler), ti-scheduler = (if q.i2-hr-scheduler >= 0 then q.i2-hr-scheduler else r.ti-scheduler), ti-steps = r.ti-steps, ti-cfg = r.ti-cfg, ti-seed = r.ti-seed, ti-width = r.ti-width, ti-height = r.ti-height, ti-out = r.ti-out, ti-params = r.ti-params, ti-clip-skip = r.ti-clip-skip, ti-extras = r.ti-extras }